  <h4>Warranty</h4>
  <p>Our Signature blinds and curtains are backed by a lifetime warranty. Look for the word "Signature" in the product name to identify these items. To avail the warranty service, the purchaser must return the damaged blind, along with the invoice or original sales receipt, to the store of purchase. Alternatively, our home repair service is included free of charge for one year, with call-out charges applicable thereafter.</p>
  <p>To qualify for the lifetime guarantee, product registration must be completed online at <a href="https://www.blindtex.com" target="_blank" style="color: #333; text-decoration: underline;">www.blindtex.com</a> within 30 days of ordering.</p>
  <p>All other custom-made blinds and curtains are warranted to be free from manufacturing defects in materials, mechanisms (cord locks and tilt gears), and components (brackets, wands, caps, etc.) for the first year. Sewing is a combination of hand and machine work, stitching and hemlines will never be perfectly straight as a result.</p>
  <p>Motors are covered by manufacturers' warranties: Somfy - 12 years for wired and 5 years for battery motors from the date of purchase; Blindtex - 12 years for wired motors, 2 years for battery motors from the date of purchase.</p>
  <p>Shutters are guaranteed for three years against cracking, splitting, and shrinkage under normal conditions of use. Due to the nature of paint, dye, or stain, we cannot guarantee an exact color and finish reproduction, with variations of -10% to +10% compared to samples or custom colors. Natural timber characteristics may also lead to variations in shades and textures.</p>
  <p>Warranty for faux wood blinds will be void if they are not kept in an air-conditioned environment below 40° Celsius.</p>
  <p>Lighting conditions may affect the appearance of color finishes. Products fitted in high-moisture areas like bathrooms, kitchens, or rooms with direct water contact, including rain damage, are not guaranteed unless the appropriate product has been specified.</p>
  <p>Our Flyscreen products are covered by a 3 year warranty for hardware parts and system components only. Any accidental damage to the fabric or screen caused by the user is the customer’s full responsibility. Warranty claims may require proof of purchase, and defective parts or products must be returned for inspection. Replacement parts will be new and will meet or exceed the original specifications. The decision to repair or replace a product under warranty remains at the company’s discretion. This warranty does not cover defects resulting from misuse, mishandling, improper operation or storage, or failure to follow recommended cleaning procedures.</p>

